./docs/evidence/light-axis/native-review.log:- The new product site is implemented in `app/`, `components/`, and `lib/` with Next.js 16, React 19, and strict TypeScript. The eleven locale routes are statically prerendered. `Story` is a Server Component; small menu/dialog event boundaries are Client Components, with story content passed as server-rendered children. The full reference PNGs are never served directly: `public/art/` supplies eleven exact-source PNG tiles plus smaller PNG supporting images. The FAQ/account region is one combined `09-10.png` tile. CHG-0047 keeps the first tile preloaded/high priority and later tiles lazy; old WebPs are archived under `public/art/unused-webp/`. RGBA/ICC exactness and Pro/Pro Max assembled visuals passed independent audit. CHG-0048 remains open: 3,194,801-byte first PNG decoded in 13.659 s at 4 Mbps/100 ms and fast distant scroll waited 33.88 s, so the overall performance/integration gate failed. The :3020 preview serves the new PNG build.
