./docs/evidence/png-reserve/native-review.log:MEMORY.md:9:- CHG-0057 adds a future-use reserve of 22 exact-source Adobe RGB PNG crops in `public/art/original-png/` (46,308,888 bytes). `tools/slice-background-png.py` regenerates them and `manifest.json` records source/output hashes and crop boxes. The live page still requests WebP only; Pro/Pro Max production WebKit request logs show zero reserve PNG requests. Format switching has not been implemented.
./docs/evidence/png-reserve/native-review.log:MEMORY.md:10:- CHG-0056 replaces the temporary 22 active PNG crops with WebP derived from the **current user-modified** Adobe RGB reference through an explicit LittleCMS Adobe RGB→sRGB conversion. Every full WebP carries sRGB ICC and exact source alpha; q95 is used where measured color shift stays within thresholds, with four document thumbnails lossless. The old `public/art/unused-webp/` archive and superseded active PNG crops were removed; `design/references/background.png` and the user's untracked `background_old.png` were preserved. `tools/convert-art-webp.py` regenerates the files and [color metrics](docs/evidence/art-webp/color-metrics.json); the method and alternatives are in [art color pipeline](docs/art-color-pipeline.md).
./docs/evidence/png-reserve/native-review.log:docs/art-color-pipeline.md:21:The future-use `public/art/original-png/` directory contains 22 source-exact PNG crops (46,308,888 bytes) with unchanged RGBA pixels and Adobe RGB ICC from the current references. `python3 tools/slice-background-png.py` regenerates and checks them; its `manifest.json` records crop boxes and hashes. They are not referenced by the current page. Because the folder is under `public/`, a deployment may carry those bytes even though the browser does not download them. A future network-based format selector needs its own browser color, cache, performance, and layout checks before activation.
